Phase 7 is in: `ci_crosscheck` now reads CI config, diffs it against the docs in code, and gives the fast model exactly one job — writing the paragraph above findings it cannot change.

## What I added

**[src/ci.ts](src/ci.ts)** (new) — parsers and diff:

- `parseWorkflow` — line parser for `run:` keys, handling `run: |`/`>` block scalars, single-line runs, quoted scalars, trailing comments, `\`-continued lines, and step names as context. No YAML dependency.
- `parseMakefile` — recipe lines attributed to their target, stripping make's `@`/`-`/`+` prefixes and ignoring `VAR := value` (that `(?!=)` matters).
- `parsePackageScripts` — records `npm run <name>`, not the script body (see the second bug below).
- `readCiConfig` — discovers `.github/workflows/*.{yml,yaml}` (capped at 10), root `Makefile`/`makefile`/`GNUmakefile`, and `package.json`. Missing files are a normal result; an unreadable one is warned about and skipped.
- `diffDocsAgainstCi` — one finding per action: `missing_in_ci`, `missing_in_docs`, or `mismatch`.
- `summarizeMismatches` — one fast-model call, one retry, fail-soft: a 429 costs the sentence, never the findings.

**[src/state.ts](src/state.ts)** — `docCommands` channel (every documented command, unfiltered) and `ciSummary`.

**[src/extract.ts](src/extract.ts)** — returns `documented` alongside the mode-filtered steps.

**[src/graph.ts](src/graph.ts)** — real `ci_crosscheck` node; the report stub renders a `## CI cross-check` section so you can see the output before Phase 8.

## Three bugs the real runs exposed

**1. `--mode user` produced false "missing in docs" claims.** The first fixture run reported *"CI lints but the docs don't mention it"* — the docs did mention it; the Phase 4 mode filter had dropped `npm run lint` from `steps`. CI is contributor-facing, so the diff now runs against `docCommands`, which keeps every block the extractor labelled. Same fixture, after the fix, has no lint finding.

**2. package.json script bodies are not comparable.** Comparing `"lint": "eslint ."` against a documented `npm run lint` reports a mismatch on every repo that defines scripts in JavaScript. Scripts are now recorded as their invocation (`npm run lint`), and `normalizeCommand` treats `npm test` ≡ `npm run test`.

**3. The first Plane run picked the wrong install.** It reported `pip3 install awscli` (one deployment job) as "what CI does", because the four `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` steps all carry the same step name and collapsed to one entry in the de-duplication. Counts are now taken before de-duplication, and `representative()` picks the most-run command.

While on Plane I also taught the classifier that script names are segmented: `check:lint`, `fix:format`, `check:types` and `pnpm turbo run check:format` are looked through to the word that carries the action.

## Verification

`npm run typecheck` and `npm run build` clean. A scratch suite (deleted) ran **70 checks, 70 passing**: parse output against a realistic multi-job workflow (block scalars, comments, `uses:`, `if:`), Makefile variable/target edge cases, 40+ `actionOf` cases, all three finding kinds, de-duplication and ordering, prompt content, and the retry/fail-soft paths with injected summarizers.

Two real end-to-end runs with your key:

```
