             pnpm turbo run build --affected     pull-request-build-lint-web-apps.yml
             pnpm turbo run check:types          pull-request-build-lint-web-apps.yml
             uv run --no-sync ruff check .       pull-request-build-lint-api.yml
             pnpm turbo run check:format         pull-request-build-lint-web-apps.yml
```

The model's prose for Plane read sensibly and invented nothing: *"The CI runs pnpm install --frozen-lockfile, but the docs never mention installing dependencies…"* No leftover containers, clones or scratch files.

## Limits

**The workflow parser is line-based.** Anchors, `${{ }}` interpolation and heredoc bodies are not resolved — a command containing `${{ matrix.x }}` is compared literally, and a heredoc body drops out of the diff entirely.

**One finding per action.** A repo that installs both npm deps and an AWS CLI gets one `install` row (the most frequent command), not two. Sub-command granularity would need a richer model than `CiAction`.

**`dev` is excluded both ways** — CI never starts a dev server, and a documented dev server is intentional, so reporting it would be noise. Documented `make install`-style umbrella targets are also classified as `other` rather than guessed.

**Only the first 10 workflow files are read**, and the diff needs at least one of the three source types to say anything — a Python repo with only `tox.ini` yields no CI commands.

