/**
 * Colour for the live progress log.
 *
 * The log is the tool's UI: one bracketed line per thing that happened. In a
 * terminal those lines are worth reading at a glance, so the tag carries the
 * phase's colour and the tokens that matter — the command that will run, the
 * status of a step, a non-zero exit code — carry their own. Everything else
 * stays default, which is what keeps the log scannable rather than a rainbow.
 *
 * The report on stdout is never coloured: it is markdown meant to be pasted
 * into an issue. Colour is also off whenever the stream is not a terminal, so
 * `npm start -- … | sed -n '/^# README/,$p'` sees exactly the bytes it saw
 * before, and NO_COLOR is honoured.
 */
```

