The log is no longer one wall of white. Every progress line is now colorized, with a hue per phase and colors for the parts that matter.

## What you'll see

| Line in your log | Now |
| --- | --- |
| `[repo] cloning …` / `[diagnose] …` / `[cli] …` | magenta tag |
| `[docker] started …` / `[ci_crosscheck] …` / `[setup] …` | blue tag |
| `[discover_docs] …` / `[extract_steps] …` / `[run_step] …` | cyan tag |
| `[report] …` | green tag |
| `[llm] …` / `[docs] …` / `[env] …` | dim gray tag |
| `[run_step] s2 $ bun run build` | the command itself in cyan |
| `-> pass` / `-> fail` / `-> skip` / `-> workaround` | green / red / yellow / yellow |
| `(exit 0, 0.4s)` vs `(exit 127, 0.1s)` | quiet gray, with the code green or red |
| `[report] 4 step(s), 2 failure(s)` | `2 failure(s)` red when non-zero |
| `Warning:` lines (`[llm] rate limited…`, `[extract_steps] LLM budget exhausted…`) | whole line yellow, on stderr |
| `Docker daemon unreachable…` | red |
| `Testing docs for …` header | bold cyan; the `Run id …; budgets:` line is dim gray |

## How it works

[src/log.ts](src/log.ts) is the whole change. Every progress line already had the shape `[phase] message`, so the module parses that shape instead of requiring a new call signature: `infoLine()` colors the tag by phase and decorates the body, `warnLine()` and `errorLine()` color whole lines on stderr, `heading()`/`muted()` handle the two header lines and the closing `Run: …` summary. I then swapped the ~34 `console.log`/`console.warn` call sites over to it — [src/graph.ts:66](src/graph.ts#L66) is the funnel for all node lines (`setup`, `discover_docs`, `extract_steps`, `run_step`, `diagnose`, `ci_crosscheck`, `report`), and docker/repo/ci/llm/extract/docs/diagnose/report/env/run/index each got the matching helper.

Two deliberate constraints:

- **The report stays plain.** `console.log("
" + reportMarkdown)` is untouched — it's the markdown artifact you paste into an issue, so no ANSI ever enters it.
- **Color switches itself off when the stream isn't a terminal.** So `npm start -- … | sed -n '/^# README/,$p'` and `> report.md` produce exactly the bytes they produced before this change, `grep '^\['` still matches, and `NO_COLOR` is honored. `FORCE_COLOR=1` overrides for cases where you want color in a pipe.

